-- ============================================================================
-- Seed data: reference tables exported from the previous Supabase project
-- with scripts/dump-data.sql.
--
-- Apply AFTER supabase/migrations/00000000000000_baseline.sql. Re-runnable:
-- every other table's statements use ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING.
--
-- 1202 rows across ten tables (woreda, woreda_settings, kebele, service_type,
-- fee_schedule, tenant_module_config, role_permission, id_card_template,
-- id_card_template_field, id_card_template_field_draft). role_permission is
-- the one that matters most:
-- without its rows no role resolves any permission, and every sign-in fails
-- in a way that looks like broken auth rather than missing data.
-- super_admin and tenant_admin are absent by design — those are decided by
-- is_super_admin() and is_tenant_admin(), not by this table.
--
-- role_permission's 972 rows are the one exception to "DO NOTHING": they use
-- ON CONFLICT ... DO UPDATE SET is_granted = EXCLUDED.is_granted instead.
-- 00000000000015_permission_matrix_backfill.sql added a trigger that
-- pre-populates every new woreda's role_permission rows from
-- default_role_perms() -- which runs during THIS script's own `woreda`
-- inserts above, before these role_permission inserts below ever execute.
-- Two hand-maintained copies of the same matrix (this seed and
-- default_role_perms()) already disagreed on a handful of cells (verified:
-- credential.verify for finance_clerk/auditor/viewer, seeded false here vs.
-- true in default_role_perms()) -- "DO NOTHING" would let the trigger's
-- value win a fresh deploy silently, contradicting what this file explicitly
-- seeds and reopening exactly the kind of drift docs/rbac-security-forensic-
-- review.md's F8 finding is about. DO UPDATE makes this file's own explicit
-- values authoritative again on a fresh deploy, matching this script's
-- pre-existing behavior (it used to be the only writer). The five permission
-- groups this file predates (F4) aren't mentioned here at all, so the
-- trigger's rows for those stand untouched either way.
--
-- updated_by columns are NULL throughout: they reference app_user, which is
-- seeded separately via scripts/dump-app-users.sql because user ids differ
-- between projects.
-- ============================================================================


-- ===== woreda (6 rows) =====

-- ===== kebele (19 rows) =====

-- ===== woreda_settings (6 rows) =====

-- ===== role_permission (972 rows) =====

-- ===== service_type (78 rows) =====

